    "plan_draft": "## Diagnosis summary\n\nLate blight is present across 57.9% of scored tomato tiles, with a broad infection front moving south-east. [doc_04#p1]\n\n## Immediate action (next 24 hours)\n\nRemove and destroy the worst affected foliage before spraying; do not leave it on field margins or compost it. [doc_12#p3]\nApply mancozeb at 2.0-2.5 g per litre over affected rows and a two-row buffer, following the product label and local extension guidance. [doc_12#p4]\nSpray early morning or late evening and avoid rain expected within four hours. [doc_07#p2]\n\n## Follow-up\n\nInspect the buffer after 3 days and re-scan after 7 days. Alternate modes of action if continued disease pressure requires later treatment. [doc_19#p1]",
